WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.640
Gibs hears Liza’s childcare concern. One first step: ask the midwife about scheduling. No appointment is promised.

2
00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:19.660
With Jo, hear her concern and respect choice. If she wants, identify a qualified contact through the health team. Gibs does not choose a method.

3
00:00:19.960 --> 00:00:31.480
With Ben, listen without diagnosing. Identify a qualified contact; the time is unconfirmed. In real immediate danger, do not delay help for an ordinary interview.

4
00:00:31.780 --> 00:00:43.300
With Ramon, ask permission and hear his goal. Gibs does not give or choose medicine. First identify the health-team contact and check understanding.

5
00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:56.440
In triads, everyone tries the BHW role. Ask for the step in their own words. Repair misunderstanding and recheck. Peer feedback is practice, not a facilitator grade.

6
00:00:56.740 --> 00:01:12.580
“Do I have an appointment tomorrow?” Liza asks. “Not yet. First we will ask about scheduling,” Gibs clarifies. On recheck, Liza says, “Ask first; no appointment yet.” “Yes, that is the first step,” Gibs confirms.
